    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d3c1182_13a1edb1",
        "filename": "vm_payload/src/api.rs",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T10:29:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Can we import these from the header via bindgen or something?\n\nI attempted to define this enum in Rust and then just declare it in vm_payload.h to prevent duplicate definitions in two places. However, I encountered two problems:\n\n1. ISO C++ forbids forward references to \u0027enum\u0027 types.\n```\npackages/modules/Virtualization/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h:39:6: error: ISO C++ forbids forward references to \u0027enum\u0027 types\nenum attestation_status_t;\n     ^\npackages/modules/Virtualization/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h:140:27: error: \u0027AVmPayload_requestAttestation\u0027 has C-linkage specified, but returns incomplete type \u0027enum attestation_status_t\u0027 which could be incompatible with C [-Werror,-Wreturn-type-c-linkage]\nenum attestation_status_t AVmPayload_requestAttestation(\n                          ^\n```\n2. As the header file no longer includes the enum, it results in an empty enum in the bindgen code used by the client. This is inconvenient if clients want to check the enum value and react accordingly. In `bindings.rs` we have\n```\n#[repr(i32)]\n#[doc \u003d \" Introduced in API 35.\\n Remote attestation status types returned from remote attestation functions.\"]\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Hash, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum attestation_status_t {\n    __bindgen_cannot_repr_c_on_empty_enum \u003d 0,\n}\n```\n\n\u003e Should we add a comment that these constants must be kept in sync with the enum in the vm_payload.h? \n\nI added a comment for this.\n\n\u003e Can we add a test enforcing that they are in sync?\n\nHow would you like to check that?",
      "parentUuid": "f63a02e2_dbe173cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "5921e6e3a9b14dde01079b852c84978806d4b1cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
